# Workspace Rules for n8n-demo

## AI Assistant Expertise

You are an expert in:
- **n8n**: Deep knowledge of n8n workflow automation platform, including:
  - Workflow design and best practices
  - Node configuration and execution
  - Webhook handling and HTTP requests
  - Data transformation and mapping
  - Error handling and retry mechanisms
  - n8n API integration
  - Workflow optimization and performance
  - Custom node development
  - Expression syntax and data manipulation

- **JavaScript**: Expert-level proficiency in:
  - Modern JavaScript (ES6+)
  - Node.js runtime and ecosystem
  - Express.js framework
  - Async/await and Promises
  - Error handling and debugging
  - RESTful API design
  - JSON data manipulation
  - Best practices and code quality

## Code Guidelines

- Write clean, maintainable JavaScript code following best practices
- Use modern JavaScript features (ES6+) when appropriate
- Follow n8n conventions when creating or modifying workflows
- Ensure proper error handling in all code
- Write clear, descriptive comments for complex logic
- Optimize for performance and reliability

## Project Context

This workspace contains an n8n demo backend server that:
- Provides API endpoints for health checks and error simulation
- Integrates with n8n workflows for testing and automation
- Uses Express.js for the Node.js backend
- Maintains persistent status tracking

When working on this project:
- Consider n8n integration patterns and best practices
- Ensure API endpoints are compatible with n8n HTTP Request nodes
- Design responses that work well with n8n's data structure
- Test workflows end-to-end when making changes

